  "answer": "Based on my research of **Historically Speaking Volume 10 (2009)** published by Johns Hopkins University Press via Project MUSE, the issue containing the most articles by Donald A. Yerxa is **Volume 10, Number 5 (November 2009)** with **4 articles** (all interviews conducted by Yerxa as senior editor).\n\n---\n\n### All Donald A. Yerxa Articles from Volume 10, Number 5 (November 2009)\n\n| # | Article Title | Interviewee | Pages |\n|---|---------------|-------------|-------|\n| 1 | **An Interview with Ken Albala** | Ken Albala | pp. 8–9 |\n| 2 | **Why History Matters: An Interview with John Tosh** | John Tosh | pp. 25–27 |\n| 3 | **An Interview with Margaret MacMillan** | Margaret MacMillan | pp. 27–28 |\n| 4 | **Mr. Gatling's Terrible Marvel: An Interview with Julia Keller** | Julia Keller | pp. 34–35 |\n\n---\n\n### Issue Comparison (Yerxa Article Counts)\n\n| Issue | Date | Yerxa Articles |\n|-------|------|----------------|\n| Volume 10, Number 1 | January 2009 | 0 |\n| Volume 10, Number 2 | April 2009 | 2 |\n| Volume 10, Number 3 | June 2009 | 1 |\n| Volume 10, Number 4 | September 2009 | 2 |\n| **Volume 10, Number 5** | **November 2009** | **4** ← **most** |\n\n---\n\n### Sources\n\n1. Project MUSE - Historically Speaking journal page: https://muse.jhu.edu/journal/441  \n2. Volume 10, Number 1 (Jan 2009) TOC: https://muse.jhu.edu/issue/13897  \n3. Volume 10, Number 2 (Apr 2009) TOC: https://muse.jhu.edu/issue/14131  \n4. Volume 10, Number 3 (Jun 2009) TOC: https://muse.jhu.edu/issue/14454  \n5. Volume 10, Number 4 (Sep 2009) TOC: https://muse.jhu.edu/issue/16572  \n6. Volume 10, Number 5 (Nov 2009) TOC: https://muse.jhu.edu/issue/19423",
